'''''Echeveria purpusiorum''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Crassulaceae]], endemic to [[Puebla]] and [[Oaxaca]], [[Mexico]].

== Description ==
''Echeveria purpusiorum'' have pointy, oval, and thick leaves with about {{convert|1.6|in|mm}} long and {{convert|1|in|mm}} wide.<ref>{{Cite web|title=International Crassulaceae Network|url=https://www.crassulaceae.ch/de/artikel?akID=48&aaID=2&aiID=P&aID=431|access-date=2021-02-03|website=www.crassulaceae.ch}}</ref> The leaves color is deep olive-green, grey-green, or white-green, with red-brown markings. The rosette slowly grows up to {{convert|3.2|in|mm}} tall and {{convert|3.2|in|mm}} in diameter. The flowers color is scarlet red, with yellow tips and bloom in late-spring with {{convert|12|in|mm}} long stem.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2014-07-04|title=Echeveria purpusorum|url=https://worldofsucculents.com/echeveria-purpusorum/|access-date=2021-02-03|website=World of Succulents|language=en-US}}</ref>

